From: fpvOS developers
Subject: [PATCH] ae: exposure in the sensor's mode, not only 1080p60's lines

The exposure table counts 1080p60 lines (14.8 us). The sensor's subdevice
now gives the mode: the line from its width, horizontal blanking and pixel
rate (unless --line-ns is given), and the longest exposure from its exposure
control's range. Table lines become the same exposure time in the mode's
lines, and an exposure longer than the mode's frame is held at its longest,
the gain making up the rest as under --max-exposure-us. At 1080p60 the line
is the table's own and the limit stays 1114: nothing changes.

Upstream: not submitted

